      "side": 1,
      "message": "**The Issue:**\nIn `cli.cc`, the `SendEcCommandAndReadResponse` function reads data from the USB bulk endpoint. Because USB bulk transfers often pad packets to a specific boundary (like 64 bytes), the `initial_buffer` might pull in the 8-byte `ec_host_response` header plus 56 bytes of payload data, even if the EC only intended to send back a 4-byte response (`resp.data_len \u003d\u003d 4`).\n\nCurrently, the code properly fetches *more* data if `response_data.size() \u003c resp.data_len`, but it doesn\u0027t trim the vector if the initial read grabbed too much. This means the caller could receive trailing garbage data.\n\n**The Fix:**\nYou just need to enforce the exact payload size right before returning the data.\n\nIn `util/focaltech/cli.cc`, at the end of `SendEcCommandAndReadResponse` (around line 117):\n\n**Current Code:**\n\n```cpp\n    response_data.insert(response_data.end(), additional.begin(),\n                         additional.end());\n  }\n\n  return response_data;\n}\n\n```\n\n**Updated Code:**\n\n```cpp\n    response_data.insert(response_data.end(), additional.begin(),\n                         additional.end());\n  }\n\n  // USB bulk reads may return padded packets. Ensure we only return the exact \n  // payload length the EC specified in its header.\n  if (response_data.size() \u003e resp.data_len) {\n    response_data.resize(resp.data_len);\n  }\n\n  return response_data;\n}\n\n```",
